35,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"The office charges 4,200 yen hourly, billed to one person. The firm requires surfaces be clear. We need a cost-sharing mechanism.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,The timing confirms my fears. A full pass takes over an hour. The inconsistent standards mean we are constantly redoing work.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"The calendar shows two people away weekly, one gone all August. Yet standards vary wildly. We’re paying for presence, not actual labor.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,May,,"Eleven days. That’s all the grout lasted before the black spots returned. Plus, we’re wasting money on duplicate spray. This room is a disaster.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Midori,,"@May, that grout sounds awful. I found our chat rows started with reminders, and the previous tenants stopped speaking. We must avoid that silence.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Ryuji, an hour weekly is manageable. @Benjamin, the billing structure is the real risk. We need a transparent ledger to prevent one person from absorbing all costs.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Ryuji"",""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Toshio, one hour is the floor, not the ceiling. With inconsistent standards, that hour becomes three. We must define ""done"" before assigning hours.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Ryuji, exactly. If ""done"" is subjective, the hour is meaningless. We need a fixed checklist so presence actually correlates with effort.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,May,,"@Benjamin, a checklist is great, but it won’t fix the mold. @Ryuji, if we define “done” as “no black spots,” we’re actually solving the real problem.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Benjamin"",""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@May, I agree. Let’s define “done” clearly to prevent resentment. @Toshio, how do we share costs fairly?","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""May"",""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Midori, I propose a shared digital ledger. Every purchase is logged immediately, and we settle balances on the first of each month.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Toshio, a ledger tracks money, not labor. I need a fixed checklist to ensure the hour is actually spent, not just claimed.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Ryuji, agreed. But @Toshio, the ledger must account for absence. If someone is gone, their share shouldn’t vanish; it should redistribute to those actually present.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Ryuji"",""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,May,,"@Benjamin, redistributing absence is fair. But @Ryuji, please make the checklist specific. I need to know exactly what “no black spots” means for my peace of mind.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Benjamin"",""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Midori,,"@Benjamin, that redistribution idea is kind. @May, let’s keep the checklist simple so we don’t argue over tiny details.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Benjamin"",""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Toshio,,"@Benjamin, absence redistribution is essential. @Midori, simplicity prevents conflict. I will draft the ledger rules to ensure no one absorbs unexpected costs.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Benjamin"",""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,"@Toshio, the ledger is necessary, but it doesn't solve the labor bottleneck. I need the checklist to be non-negotiable. If standards remain subjective, the time cost triples.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"@Ryuji, agreed. @Toshio, let’s combine these. A fixed checklist defines the work, and the ledger redistributes costs based on actual presence. That balances fairness with reality.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Ryuji"",""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,May,,"@Benjamin, that sounds solid. @Ryuji, please make the checklist specific. I need to know exactly what “no black spots” means for my peace of mind.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Benjamin"",""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Midori,,"@May, I’ll keep the checklist gentle to protect our friendship. @Toshio, let’s ensure the ledger feels fair, not like a punishment.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""May"",""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
